BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Patchwork: Connecticut Artists Consider 250
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260627
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261109
DTSTAMP:20261010T160618Z
UID:e0bfea214e6c7c09aeb09fdcedf5@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:In June 2026\, the Florence Griswold Museum will mount a jurie
 d exhibition of contemporary art to celebrate the 250th birthday of the Un
 ited States of America. Museums and cultural institutions across the natio
 n are marking this anniversary in myriad ways. As the historic home of the
  Lyme Art Colony (1900–1937)\, the Museum will highlight its legacy of s
 upporting contemporary artists by inviting today’s Connecticut-based art
 ists to submit work that addresses themes of American identity and history
  over the country’s past 250 years.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/event
 s/patchwork-connecticut-artists-consider-250
LOCATION:Florence Griswold Museum\, 96 Lyme Street\, Old Lyme CT\, 06371
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/patchwork-connecticut-artists-consider-250
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
