BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Snow Goose
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260828
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261019
DTSTAMP:20261010T160618Z
UID:d7dfb517017918bc91154e4caf72@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:On the windswept coast of England an unlikely bond forms betwe
 en Philip\, a reclusive artist shunned by society\, and Frith\, a resilien
 t young woman\, when they rescue a wounded snow goose. With World War II l
 ooming\, their friendship allows her to imagine a life beyond her village
 \, and him to confront his own humanity as he sets sail on a daring journe
 y to save soldiers trapped at Dunkirk. Discover an unforgettable new music
 al with a soaring score that will fill your heart.\n\nSource: https://ctvi
 sit.com/events/snow-goose
LOCATION:The Goodspeed\, 6 Main Street\, East Haddam CT\, 06423
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/snow-goose
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Connecticut Renaissance Faire
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260829
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
DTSTAMP:20261010T160618Z
UID:82091beb6910ab41632e6d6404ee@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:The Connecticut Renaissance Faire returns to the Lebanon Fairg
 rounds from August 29 through October 25\, 2026\, running every Saturday a
 nd Sunday plus Labor Day and Columbus Day. Nine weekends and two holiday M
 ondays of full-contact jousting\, artisan markets\, live entertainment\, p
 eriod food and drink\, and the kind of spectacle that draws tens of thousa
 nds to Lebanon each fall. Each weekend runs on its own distinct theme: Dra
 gons & Dungeons\, Faerie Ring Revels\, Pirates & Vikings\, Shirefolk\, and
  five others. New shows\, new shops\, changing menus. It's not the same fa
 ire twice.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/connecticut-renaissance-f
 aire-2
LOCATION:Lebanon Fairgrounds\, 122 Mack Road\, Lebanon CT\, 06249
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/connecticut-renaissance-faire-2
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:"Field Notes" Works by Eve Biddle
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260902
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261019
DTSTAMP:20261010T160618Z
UID:7acbe1185ca40df7723f3a8023dc@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:The Tremaine Gallery at Hotchkiss presents Field Notes\, an ex
 hibition of works by contemporary artist Eve Biddle\, curated by Terri Moo
 re. Drawing on the symbolism of snakes as signs of life and fertility and 
 referencing archaeological artifacts across time\, Biddle's work explores 
 the ways memory\, perception\, and presence transform our understanding of
  the natural world. Her images follow a meandering path\, reminding us tha
 t neither history nor our own lives move in straight lines. Nature appears
  ambiguously alive or dead\, abstracted and literal at once.\n\nSource: ht
 tps://ctvisit.com/events/field-notes-works-eve-biddle
LOCATION:Tremaine Art Gallery at The Hotchkiss School\, 11 Interlaken Road
 \, Lakeville CT\, 06039
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/field-notes-works-eve-biddle
END:VEVENT
